  "notes": "Modified cash basis village (Sept 30 FYE). Governmental lines are the Total column of the governmental funds statement of revenues, expenditures and changes in fund balances (p6-7); beginning/ending cash = fund balance (cash) on p7 (414,081 / 507,337, which equal cash in bank + cash at county treasurer on p5). Transfers in 45,522 and out 36,328 are the Total column after the Adjustment column removed 53,568 of interfund transfers (net 9,194 to business-type funds). Business-type lines come from the Proprietary Funds Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Fund Net Position, Totals column (p9); measure = net position (362,269 to 346,762), transfers net -9,194; no single total printed, so receipts (159,666) and disbursements (165,979) are sums of printed lines. Depreciation (non-cash) is included in business-type disbursements as printed. Business-type disbursements are listed by object and all mapped to utilities. Cash flow statement (p10) shows beginning cash 89,016 and ending 71,012 for enterprise funds; not used as proprietary is null (cash basis). Detail left empty on purpose: the only supplementary schedule (Budgetary Comparison Schedule - Cash Basis, Total Primary Government, p11-12) combines governmental and business-type funds, lumps business-type receipts into 'Other' (283,235), includes transfers in 135,418 and transfers in disbursements, and does not split by fund type, so it cannot be recorded without mixing fund types. Read pages 1-12 of 12."
